From: perf session 2026-09-11
Subject: [PATCH 0022] wasm64: the goto_ptr handoff slot was read at the wrong offset (every indirect jump unwound to cpu_exec_loop)

tcg_out_goto_ptr stores the next TB's descriptor at [sp-8] with
sp = frame+16, i.e. frame+8; the dispatcher read frame+0 (always 0),
so W64_EXIT_GOTOPTR always looked like a lookup miss: every indirect
jump (bx lr, pop {pc}, ldr pc) returned to cpu_exec_loop for a fresh
tb_lookup + cpu_loop_exec_tb instead of continuing in the dispatcher
loop.  Temporary exit-kind counters over a 30 s boot: 16.8M dispatcher
exits, 14.9M of them goto_ptr "misses", 0 hits.  Read frame+8 and treat
tcg_code_gen_epilogue as the miss value.

Measured (idlebench --quick vs the 0021 dist, both orders):
  window 24.3 -> 21.9 (-10 %) / 23.7 -> 21.9 (-8 %)
  t0.5G  39.1 -> 37.6 (-4 %) / 38.6 -> 37.1 (-4 %)
  t1.3G  57.6 -> 54.5 (-5 %) / 55.7 -> 54.5 (-2 %)
Gates: op-suite wasm64 1156/1156, lockstep 250e6 clean, Firefox idle.

diff --git a/tcg/wasm64/wasm64.c b/tcg/wasm64/wasm64.c
--- a/tcg/wasm64/wasm64.c	2026-09-11 09:54:24.016735104 +0000
+++ b/tcg/wasm64/wasm64.c	2026-09-11 09:49:32.955895253 +0000
@@ -1906,8 +1906,11 @@
         }
 
         if (res & W64_EXIT_GOTOPTR) {
-            uintptr_t next = *(uintptr_t *)w64_frame;
-            if (next == 0) {
+            /* the handoff slot is [sp-8] = frame+8 (sp = frame+16); the
+             * dispatcher read frame+0 — always 0 — so every goto_ptr
+             * unwound to cpu_exec_loop (14.9M of 16.8M exits per boot) */
+            uintptr_t next = *(uintptr_t *)(w64_frame + 8);
+            if (next == 0 || next == (uintptr_t)tcg_code_gen_epilogue) {
                 return 0;
             }
             tb = next;
